# Python
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# LaTeX build products (docs/)
docs/**/*.aux
docs/**/*.log
docs/**/*.out
docs/**/*.toc
docs/**/*.fls
docs/**/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/**/*.synctex.gz
docs/**/*.lof
docs/**/*.lot

# Isaac Lab run output if launched from here
logs/
outputs/

# Diagnostic output. play_dig.py, render_dig.py and mpm_minimal_probe.py all
# default their --trace, --dump and --json paths to the working directory, so a
# session's worth of parked runs leaves a few dozen of these in the repo root.
# They are regenerable, and leaving them untracked blocks `git pull --rebase`
# on a dirty tree, which has already cost a rebuild loop.
dig_*.csv
dig_*.npz
dig_*.gif
dig_*.png
goal_trace.csv
goals.png
setpoint.png

# Training console output. One file, overwritten each run: the numbered
# variants only ever accumulated dead logs nobody reads.
train.log

# The converted excavator asset and the stamp recording which excavator.py it
# was built from. Both are generated on the machine that runs, by write_mjcf
# then convert_mjcf, and neither is tracked. The USD once was -- committed on
# one box, never pushed -- while the stamp was not, so every
# `git checkout -- .` put that old build back under a stamp that still matched
# the current source: the one case the stamp exists to catch, passed.
assets/excavator/
assets/excavator.usd.srchash
